n put in all kinds  of different antibodies we've played  around with different liter peptides and  every time we throw something at this  system I'd say probably nine times out  of ten we get we get a really great  yield and we get a clean molecule that  does everything it's supposed to do so  to finish I just like to first  acknowledge my boss Steve dowdy that's a  picture of him surfing he's awesome I  love working for Steve he has a lot of  great ideas he's very supportive and  he's an eternal optimist these are  various members of the lab who've worked  on the si RNA project over the last few  years I'd like to point out are Ian van  der Bannon Berg who is now scientists at  thermo he did most of the expression  experiments in this talk that I showed  you today and he taught me what I know  about working with XP Cho and then these  two grad students Alex and Aaron did a  lot of the animal work and optimization  of the conjugation chemistry's so  finally I want to thank the guys at  thermo for working so closely with us  and for inviting me giving me a chance  to talk to you tonight  you  Thank You dr. Huggins for your  informative presentation now if you have  any  dr. Huggins please type them in the ask  question box and click send dr. Huggins  will be answering questions via the  email address you provided at the time  of registration we would like to thank  lab roots and our sponsor  Thermo Fisher Scientific for  underwriting today's educational webcast  webcast can be viewed on-demand and  labret swill alert you via email when  it's available for replay we encourage  you to share that email with your  colleagues who may have missed today's  live event  you will now be redirected to the  registration page of our next webinar  expression purification and  characterization of difficult to express  membrane proteins in the XV 293 and  éxito expression systems a case study of  potassium chloride cotransporter KCC -  presented by dr. unasked Johari on  September 